      "idempotency": "forbidden",
      "focuses": false,
      "queue_offline": false,
      "remote_relay": "deny",
      "input": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {}
      },
      "output": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "signedIn": {
            "type": "boolean"
          },
          "team": {
            "type": [
              "string",
              "null"
            ]
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "signedIn"
        ]
      },
      "cli": {
        "path": "auth status",
        "visible": true
      },
      "mcp": {
        "expose": "default",
        "group": "cloud"
      },
      "docs": "Whether cmux is signed in to cmux Cloud and which team requests use. cmux answers from its own sign-in; the app server never sees a token.",
      "since": "cloud/1"
    },
    {
      "name": "cloud.machine.watch",
      "owner": "app:cmux/cloud",
      "class": "read",
      "risk": "read",
      "idempotency": "forbidden",
      "focuses": false,
      "queue_offline": false,
      "remote_relay": "deny",
      "input": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {}
      },
      "output": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "revision": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "description": "The machine projection revision now."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "revision"
        ]
      },
      "cli": {
        "path": "machine watch",
        "visible": false
      },
      "mcp": {
        "expose": "never",
        "group": "cloud"
      },
      "docs": "The machine change stream. The catalog has no stream class yet, so this read answers the current projection revision; the server then sends cloud.machine.watch events after each op: {type: upsert, revision, machine} or {type: removed, revision, id}. One revision per projection change; no timer, no polling.",
      "since": "cloud/1"
    },
    {
      "name": "cloud.machine.connect",
      "owner": "app:cmux/cloud",
      "class": "mutation",
      "risk": "mutate-shared",
      "idempotency": "required",
      "focuses": false,
      "queue_offline": false,
      "remote_relay": "deny",
      "input": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "machine": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 128,
            "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9_-]{0,127}$",
            "description": "The machine id (vm-…) from cloud.machine.list."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "machine"
        ]
      },
      "output": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "machine": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "carrier": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "cloud-vm/<machine>#<generation>; a new id after each reconnect."
          },
          "generation": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 1
          },
          "state": {
            "const": "up"
          },
          "socket": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "The link's local socket (owner-only directory) until the host passes a carrier fd."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "machine",
          "carrier",
          "generation",
          "state",
          "socket"
        ]
      },
      "cli": {
        "path": "machine connect",
        "visible": true
      },
      "mcp": {
        "expose": "opt_in",
        "group": "cloud"
      },
      "palette": {
        "title": {
          "en": "Connect to Cloud Machine",
          "ja": "クラウドマシンに接続"
        }
      },
      "docs": "Open the one private link (carrier) to a machine and return it. A second call while the link is up returns the same carrier and starts no new link. A paused machine is started first. Not a focus change. When the link goes down nothing reconnects by itself and nothing queues: call connect again, also with the same key: connect is never replayed from the ledger.",
      "since": "cloud/1"
    },
    {
